{"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"EntityCollapse","kind":"identifier"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"content":[{"anchor":"Why-the-hook-takes-the-whole-collection","level":2,"text":"Why the hook takes the whole collection","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A per-ID resolver would only handle half the problem. Rows sharing an ","type":"text"},{"code":"id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"are one failure mode; the other is a ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"singleton","type":"text"}]},{"text":" — an entity an app holds","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"exactly one of, such as a settings record. Created independently on two","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"fresh installs, two singletons have ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"different","type":"text"}]},{"text":" UUIDs, so nothing groups","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"them and no ID-keyed resolver can ever see the conflict. A","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"([E]) -> [E]","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" hook covers both, plus general garbage collection, with one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"API.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"The-determinism-requirement","level":2,"text":"The determinism requirement","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A resolver must be a pure function of ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"replicated content","type":"text"}]},{"text":" — never","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"persistentModelID","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", never a local timestamp, never array position. Every","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"device must compute the same survivor set from the same rows. A resolver","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that doesn’t reintroduces the mutual-tombstone loss the write path is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"designed to avoid: two devices pick different survivors, each tombstones the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"other’s, and after sync ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"both","type":"text"}]},{"text":" rows are gone.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"It must also be idempotent — ","type":"text"},{"code":"collapse(collapse(rows))","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" must keep the same","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"IDs as ","type":"text"},{"code":"collapse(rows)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". This is checked with an ","type":"text"},{"code":"assert","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in debug builds.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Collapse-removes-IDs-not-rows","level":2,"text":"Collapse removes IDs, not rows","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A resolver’s output is read as ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"the set of IDs that should exist and what","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"each should contain","type":"text"}]},{"text":". An ID the resolver drops is deleted, including every","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"row carrying it. Several rows that share a ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"surviving","type":"text"}]},{"text":" ID are all updated","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to the survivor’s value, and none of them is deleted.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"That asymmetry is deliberate, and it is the whole reason the singleton case","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is the one this hook really solves. Deleting an ID is safe because ","type":"text"},{"code":"id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"replicated: every device independently computes the same set of doomed IDs","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and issues the same deletions. Deleting one of several rows that share an ID","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"not","type":"text"}]},{"text":" safe — nothing replicated distinguishes them, so two devices can","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"pick different physical rows to keep, each tombstones the other’s, and both","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"are lost.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Rows sharing an ID need no deletion anyway: writes already converge across","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"every matching row and reads already collapse to one value per ID (see","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/EntityDB","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":"), so duplicates cost storage and nothing else.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"kind":"symbol","metadata":{"symbolKind":"enum","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"EntityCollapse","kind":"identifier"}],"externalID":"s:17SwiduxPersistence14EntityCollapseO","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"EntityCollapse","kind":"identifier"}],"roleHeading":"Enumeration","title":"EntityCollapse","role":"symbol","modules":[{"name":"SwiduxPersistence"}]},"abstract":[{"text":"Ready-made collapse resolvers.","type":"text"}],"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Type-Methods","title":"Type Methods","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiduxPersistence\/documentation\/SwiduxPersistence\/EntityCollapse\/byID(preferring:)"]}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swiduxpersistence\/entitycollapse"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"iden